@packages/core/src/model/retrieval.sigil from SigilRetrievalModel import { RetrievalProjection }

component SigilRetrievalMarkdown {
  goal {
    Render one compact, deterministic Markdown document from a versioned retrieval
    projection so people and coding agents can inspect a component contract and its
    direct relationships without reconstructing flat evidence.
  }

  interface {
    RetrievalMarkdownProjection {
      SigilRetrievalModel RetrievalProjection provides the sole presentation input.

      renderRetrieveMarkdown(projection) returns one Markdown document without
      changing the projection, raw PurposeRetrievalResult, or either fingerprint.

      The sole document title is the projection purpose value, one space, and the
      word retrieval. Each selected-role RetrievedComponent then renders in
      projection order. Its heading is the component name. Its repository-relative
      declaration path follows as a Source line whose text is Source, colon, space,
      then the path. Zero selected-role components omit that block and still render
      related groups, Diagnostics, and Glossary when present.

      Each selected component renders Goal, Interface, State, Logic, Constraints,
      Decisions, Cases, Ownership, and Links in that order when each section has
      content. Each Goal, State, Logic, Constraints, Decisions, and Cases Facet is
      one list entry whose content is that unit's semantic text. Each Interface Facet
      is one list entry of that unit's semantic text under Interface or under its Tag
      heading.

      Interface content renders under a Tag heading only when the projection carries
      an authored local grouping identity. Ungrouped Facets remain directly under
      Interface, even when they introduce or reference Tags inline.

      Related components render after selected components in role order:
      Dependencies, Importers, then Cycle members. Each present role has one group
      heading; a missing role emits no heading. Explicit summaries follow these
      ordinary roles.

      Each related component heading is its name, followed by its repository-relative
      Source line and stable Identity line. It renders Goal and Interface with
      emphasis labels when those sections contain Facets. Each Facet is one list
      entry; Interface uses the same authored local grouping rule as a selected
      component.

      OwnershipLinks without Tag scope render in the consumer component Ownership
      section. A Tag-scoped link renders under a matching authored Interface grouping
      when present; otherwise it renders in Ownership with explicit Tag and
      originating-owner labels. Never fabricate an Interface group, duplicate a link,
      or erase its Tag scope. Each advisory implements, uses, or tests link retains
      the existing one-way path/line/column Markdown link, optional symbol, and
      selected sections. That implementation link promises neither completeness nor
      current alignment. Omit Ownership when no link is assigned there.

      Projection diagnostics render after related groups and before Glossary. Each
      diagnostic is one list entry using the stable human text of severity, code, and
      message without path or range. An empty diagnostic collection emits no heading.

      Glossary terms from the projection render last as one Glossary list. Each term
      is one list entry whose text is the term in strong emphasis, space, em dash,
      space, then the definition. A missing glossary emits no heading.
    }
  }

  constraints {

    OwnershipLinkEncoding {
      Each Ownership list entry uses the relation, a Markdown link labeled path colon
      line colon column and targeting path hash L line, an optional parenthesized
      symbol, then colon and selected section names separated by comma space. For a
      Tag-scoped entry in Ownership append semicolon, space, Tag colon space and the
      exact Tag name, then semicolon, space, Origin colon space and its source
      path/component identity. Apply the existing Markdown escaping rules. This label
      describes annotation scope and does not declare a Tag.
    }

    AnnotationScopePresentation {
      Ordinary Interface Facets group only under authored local grouping Tags. Render
      advisory annotation Tag scope separately under its consumer component when no
      matching local group exists, preserving exact accessible Tag spelling and
      originating owner. Imported and inline-only Tags never become fabricated local
      declarations or whole-component implementation claims.

      Location labels retain the projection one-way line/column display; source
      navigation uses the corresponding coordinate kind and captured identity, with
      conversion from Sigil byte ranges against the matching snapshot.
    }

    RetrievalMarkdownProjection {
      Use ATX depth 1 for the document title, depth 2 for each selected component and
      for Dependencies, Importers, Cycle members, Diagnostics, and Glossary, depth 3
      for selected section titles and related component names, and depth 4 for Tag
      identities. A selected component heading is the component name. Related
      emphasis labels are Goal, Interface, Constraints, and Decisions wrapped as
      Markdown strong emphasis. List entries use a hyphen marker. A Links entry
      writes source identity, space, two hyphens, relation name, two hyphens,
      greater-than, space, then target identity.

      Do not emit a Goal or Interface heading under a related component. Do not emit
      a heading per glossary term.

      Render remaining selected-component graph relations as an ordered list. Each
      entry uses that same Links grammar. Omit origin location. Omit a selected-
      declaration relation. Omit the Links heading when no remaining relations exist.

      Do not render raw EvidenceKind labels, a matching expansion heading, an
      implementation-source text or range slice, a duplicate ordinary project summary
      contract, empty-section placeholders, or a separate presentation relationship
      map. An ordinary summary uses its ordinary selected or related component role;
      no Module Context category is inferred.

      Preserve projection ordering. Escape only backslash, backtick, asterisk,
      underscore, left square bracket, and right square bracket by prefixing a
      backslash. After that encoding is parsed, semantic text, locations, component
      identity, and link targets are unchanged.
    }
  }

  decisions {
    ComponentFirstRetrievalMarkdown {
      Decision: Render only the component-first RetrievalProjection instead of
      grouping raw retrieval evidence in the CLI formatter.

      Scope: Governs retrieve Markdown structure; excludes raw JSON retrieval,
      context Markdown compatibility, workspace rendering, and compilation reports.

      Trade-offs: Markdown depends on the maintained projection schema, while the
      renderer becomes small, deterministic, and independent of evidence selection.

      Design issues addressed: Raw evidence headings expose retrieval internals and
      make operational Facets, project summaries, and implementation source appear as
      peer human-facing sections.

      Consequences: Component and Tag ownership is visible directly, while raw
      evidence remains available only to consumers that need it.

      Revisit when: A projection field cannot express a necessary agent-facing
      retrieval decision without renderer-side semantic inference.
    }

    RelatedContractMarkdown {
      Decision: Render dependency, importer, and cycle-member contracts with
      component identity plus Goal and Interface list items, and keep Tag headings
      when the projection supplies a Tag identity. An ordinary explicitly selected
      summary exposes its selected sections using the ordinary component layout.

      Scope: Governs related-component Markdown; excludes selected-component section
      depth, raw evidence kinds, and dependency-decision prose.

      Rationale: Related contracts already carry per-unit Tag identity. Flattening
      them hides the component-owned grouping boundary that agents need.

      Trade-offs: Related sections grow longer than inline joined prose, while
      readers keep the same Tag structure as the selected component.

      Discarded alternatives: Joined Goal and Interface paragraphs and omitting
      related Tag headings were rejected after per-unit evidence landed.

      Consequences: Importers and cycle members become visible without printing
      EvidenceKind labels or repeating an ordinary project summary already shown
      elsewhere.
    }

    GlossaryMarkdown {
      Decision: Render projection glossary entries as one trailing list without a
      heading per term.

      Scope: Governs retrieve Markdown glossary presentation; excludes glossary
      selection policy and GlossaryFile authorship.

      Rationale: Selected terms are already scoped retrieval evidence. A flat list
      avoids repeating term text as a heading and a list item.

      Consequences: Markdown can show reviewed terminology only when the projection
      carries glossary entries.
    }

    DiagnosticMarkdown {
      Decision: Render projection diagnostics as one list after related groups and
      before Glossary, and omit the heading when the collection is empty.

      Scope: Governs retrieve Markdown diagnostic placement; excludes diagnostic
      selection and raw evidence diagnostic units.

      Rationale: RetrievalProjection already copies ordered diagnostics, and retrieve
      Markdown would otherwise drop failures that context Markdown reports.

      Consequences: Glossary remains last. Empty retrievals do not grow a heading.
    }
  }

  cases {
    RetrievalMarkdownProjection {
      A selected component with MarkdownOutput renders its owned operational Facets
      under MarkdownOutput while preserving their contract roles and never creating
      an expansion heading.

      An unscoped OwnershipLink renders once in the selected Ownership section. A
      Tag-scoped link renders once under an existing matching Interface group or in
      Ownership with explicit scope and origin. Ownership never renders
      implementation source text or invents a local Tag declaration.

      A selected component with no State, Logic, Constraints, Decisions, Cases, or
      component-owned OwnershipLinks omits those headings while retaining Goal,
      Interface, and present related groups.

      Two selected-role components each receive their own name, path, and selected
      sections before related groups. A diagnostics-only projection still emits the
      purpose title and Diagnostics.

      A dependency whose interface units carry RetrievalProjection renders those
      units under that Tag heading and does not join them into one paragraph.

      An ordinary project summary renders once through its explicit selected or
      related component role; its filename does not create another presentation
      category.

      An empty Importers, Cycle members, Diagnostics, or Glossary collection emits no
      group heading.

      A selected-declaration link does not appear under Links.

      An imported or inline-only Tag with an OwnershipLink and no authored Interface
      grouping renders in the consumer Ownership section with explicit Tag scope and
      origin; it creates no Interface heading or local grouping.
    }
  }
}
